{"id": "swebq0117", "pool": "swebq", "tier": "never", "audio_s": 2.09, "n_chunks": 3, "n_concurrent": 3, "gen_active_at_eot": true, "eot_score": 0.448, "eot_read_ms": 29, "reference_answer": "Mendelian inheritance", "query": "what was gregor mendel contribution?", "transcript": "Gregor Mendel's contribution?", "mode": "local", "answer": "Gregor Mendel was a scientist who did important work with pea plants. He noticed that certain traits, like plant height or seed color, were passed from parents to their children in patterns. By carefully planting and observing thousands of pea plants, he discovered the basic rules of how traits are inherited. His ideas formed the foundation of genetics, which helps us understand how living things inherit characteristics from their parents.", "answer_ms": 2576}
{"id": "swebq0120", "pool": "swebq", "tier": "never", "audio_s": 3.53, "n_chunks": 4, "n_concurrent": 4, "gen_active_at_eot": true, "eot_score": 0.3633, "eot_read_ms": 29, "reference_answer": "Government of Virginia", "query": "what was the government like in virginia colony?", "transcript": "What was the government like in Virginia colony?", "mode": "local", "answer": "Virginia Colony was a royal colony governed by the British Crown. The government was structured around a governor appointed by the king, who held significant authority over the colony. The governor was assisted by a council of advisors, often including local landowners and influential figures. Laws were based on English common law, and the colony had its own assembly, known as the House of Burgesses, which played a role in local governance but operated under strict oversight from the British authorities. Over time, tensions grew as colonists sought more autonomy, eventually leading to growing unrest that would shape the future of the American colonies.", "answer_ms": 3879}
{"id": "swebq0123", "pool": "swebq", "tier": "never", "audio_s": 2.92, "n_chunks": 3, "n_concurrent": 3, "gen_active_at_eot": true, "eot_score": 0.2483, "eot_read_ms": 29, "reference_answer": "Mathematician;Astronomer;Astrologer;Geographer;Philosopher", "query": "who was ptolemy and what did he do?", "transcript": "Who was Ptolemy, and what did he do?", "mode": "local", "answer": "Ptolemy was a scholar who studied the stars. He would sit quietly by the river and watch the sky, learning about the movements of the planets and stars.", "answer_ms": 1083}
