{"id": "swebq0174", "pool": "swebq", "tier": "never", "audio_s": 2.41, "n_chunks": 3, "n_concurrent": 3, "gen_active_at_eot": true, "eot_score": 0.1595, "eot_read_ms": 29, "reference_answer": "Sahara;Libyan Desert", "query": "what are physical features of egypt?", "transcript": "What are physical features of Egypt?", "mode": "local", "answer": "The physical features of Egypt include the Nile River, which runs through the country and supports much of its agriculture. The Sahara Desert covers most of the nation, making it one of the largest hot deserts in the world. The Nile Delta is a fertile region where the river splits into many branches before flowing into the Mediterranean Sea. Other features include rocky plateaus, oases scattered throughout the desert, and some coastal areas along the Red Sea and Mediterranean.", "answer_ms": 2889}
